Summary: regression pass on build 2026.09.21-3 finished this morning. Two issues opened, both non-blocking, both in Linear. Everything else in the smoke suite is green. Writing it up here so it is in one place; nothing needed from anyone outside eng.

1) TES-1042 - Export CSV encoding
   Severity: S3 (non-blocking; cosmetic, data intact)
   Repro:
     1. Open any plant with non-ASCII characters in a plant or machine name (test plant "Zürich Süd" works)
     2. Export > CSV
     3. Open the file in Excel on Windows
   Actual: non-ASCII plant names come out mangled ("ZÃ¼rich"). File is UTF-8 with no BOM since the streaming export change; Excel on Windows assumes the local code page without one.
   Workaround: Data > From Text, choose UTF-8.
   Owner: Omar picked it up at standup (one-liner: write the BOM).

2) TES-1043 - Dashboard date filter
   Severity: S3 (non-blocking; confusing, no data loss)
   Repro:
     1. Set the date range to a custom range, e.g. Sep 1 - Sep 14
     2. Refresh the page
   Actual: the filter resets to "last 7 days" after refresh. The persisted range is stored but the restore path does not go through the new resolver.
   Workaround: re-select the range.
   Owner: Dev, after #412 per standup.

Both are tagged for the Oct 13 patch. Neither is in the Halberd cutover path; I re-ran the Halberd smoke suite on the fixed build and it is green apart from these two.

